  "name": "Bird songs (Cahuilla, Kumeyaay and Colorado River song cycles)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song cycles of the Cahuilla, Serrano, Kumeyaay (Kumiai), Quechan, Mojave, Cocopah and neighbouring peoples of southern California, the lower Colorado River and northern Baja California, recounting in cycles of hundreds of songs the journeys of the first people and the birds, sung through the night at memorials, gatherings and celebrations. A line of men sings in unison, each shaking a gourd rattle filled with seeds, while women dance in a line before them; the Cahuilla belong to a different language family from the Yuman peoples but share the genre.",
